\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {No cheap signal grades beyond the free correctness bit: every matching metric lands in $[-0.33, +0.14]$ against blind human soundness, while the free answer-correct bit tops the entire field at $+0.92$.} Each row is one evaluation signal scored against blind human soundness on the anchor set of 60 human-graded solutions: Pearson and Spearman correlations, the within-correct correlation (restricted to solutions whose final answer is correct, the margin a grader must win), the model-ranking Spearman on hard versus saturated benchmarks, and the share of per-solution variance owned by the item (the reference). The completion curve truncates a solution, lets a fixed completer finish it, and scores whether the completion reaches the right answer; it adds no measurable grading signal beyond the free bit (Section~\ref {sec:verify}). Point estimates only; confidence intervals, subset sizes, and per-row caveats are in the twin table, Table~\ref {tab:citwin} (Appendix~\ref {app:citwin}).}}{2}{table.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:classfull}{{1}{2}{\textbf {No cheap signal grades beyond the free correctness bit: every matching metric lands in $[-0.33, +0.14]$ against blind human soundness, while the free answer-correct bit tops the entire field at $+0.92$.} Each row is one evaluation signal scored against blind human soundness on the anchor set of 60 human-graded solutions: Pearson and Spearman correlations, the within-correct correlation (restricted to solutions whose final answer is correct, the margin a grader must win), the model-ranking Spearman on hard versus saturated benchmarks, and the share of per-solution variance owned by the item (the reference). The completion curve truncates a solution, lets a fixed completer finish it, and scores whether the completion reaches the right answer; it adds no measurable grading signal beyond the free bit (Section~\ref {sec:verify}). Point estimates only; confidence intervals, subset sizes, and per-row caveats are in the twin table, Table~\ref {tab:citwin} (Appendix~\ref {app:citwin})}{table.caption.1}{}}
